---
import LabShell from "../../components/lab/LabShell.astro";
import PillarBadge from "../../components/PillarBadge.astro";
---
<LabShell title="Badges" current="badges"
  intro="Two badge patterns: the generic status .badge (global.css §6.5) and PillarBadge, the pillar-tinted capability pill used across the landing page.">

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--live">live</span>
    <h2>PillarBadge</h2>
    <p>Tissue / neural / flow — the three-capability pill. Colored from the same pillar ramp as the motifs, so
      it always stays in sync with a palette relock.</p>
    <p class="lab-source">Used in: FeatureGrid, plus 2 other landing-page spots</p>
    <div class="lab-row">
      <PillarBadge pillar="tissue" />
      <PillarBadge pillar="neural" />
      <PillarBadge pillar="flow" />
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--unused">defined, unused on real pages</span>
    <h2>Generic status badge</h2>
    <p><code>.badge</code> + <code>--success/--warning/--danger/--info</code> modifiers exist in
      <code>global.css</code> but nothing on the live site currently renders one — no status/state UI
      (payout status, application status, etc.) has been built against it yet.</p>
    <div class="lab-row">
      <span class="badge">Default</span>
      <span class="badge badge--success">Active</span>
      <span class="badge badge--warning">Pending</span>
      <span class="badge badge--danger">Failed</span>
      <span class="badge badge--info">Info</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-note">
    <strong>Gap:</strong> no Astro wrapper for the generic badge (raw <code>class="badge"</code> only). If/when
    it gets a real use (e.g. funding-opportunity status, payout status), it's worth componentizing then rather
    than now, so the API matches the actual data shape it needs to render.
  </div>
</LabShell>
